#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489245 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c28dcab-dd12-58c2-88c6-0301dc0f9ce4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rational Decimals"}] :question/id #uuid "975545b6-bff4-5fab-aaf4-e8ee01507788" :question/math-academy-id "e-22727" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are rational?\n\nI. $1.577$\n\nII. $8.163452 \\ldots$\n\nIII. $2.\\overline{73}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our numbers in turn.\n\n- $1.577$ is a rational number because it can be expressed as a ratio of two integers:\n\n$$\n1.577 = \\dfrac{1\\,577}{1\\,000}\n$$\n\n- $8.163452 \\ldots$ is not a rational number. The notation \"$\\ldots$\" tells us that digits after the decimal point extend forever. Because there is no indicated repeating pattern, this represents a non-terminating, non-repeating decimal.\n\n- $2.\\overline{73}$ is a rational number. The notation $\\overline{73}$ tells us that the digits $7$ and $3$ after the decimal point repeat indefinitely.\n\n$$\n2.\\overline{73} = 2.73737373\\ldots\n$$\n\nAny decimal with repeating digits can be represented as a ratio of two integers. In this case,\n\n$$\n2.\\overline{73}  = \\dfrac{271}{99}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489180 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Number as a Finite Decimal Using Long Division"}] :question/id #uuid "11a8381c-60e6-54f2-ac78-bece2edc403e" :question/math-academy-id "e-22733" :question/problem "Convert $\\dfrac{35}{4}$ into a decimal using long division." :question/worked-solution "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n35 \\div 4\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0$:\n\n![](images/ad/adfe6e3eeef5940412a5231d0342dfbab55c3352145b5964ced86841c920590e.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{35}{4} = 8.75.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489196 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ee93f86-38d1-591a-b694-a4f455240d75" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Number as a Repeating Decimal Using Long Division"}] :question/id #uuid "2953724f-e9c5-5a58-a253-c1d894297cc0" :question/math-academy-id "e-22734" :question/problem "Convert $\\dfrac{79}{6}$ into a repeated decimal using long division." :question/worked-solution "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n79 \\div 6\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, continuing until a repeating pattern of digits appears after the decimal point:\n\n![](images/3c/3c9add129b16a1dedeb68e0397f6345d7f481f3bbfdd54c0a35067abaaa15263.svg)\n\nWe could continue the division, but the same digit keeps repeating. Thus, the decimal continues with repeating $6$'s:\n\n$$\n13.16\\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{79}{6} = 13.16\\ldots = 13.1\\overline{6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c28dcab-dd12-58c2-88c6-0301dc0f9ce4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rational Decimals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08141af8-203c-560d-9d2f-d58a15e60119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488488} {:answer/id #uuid "21ed7e7e-47d0-51d4-9a00-b693a1f146e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488538} {:answer/id #uuid "3076fbb6-d739-5e86-8919-58296cbe6704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488573} {:answer/id #uuid "9e870dfe-4629-58ec-b281-563663104cb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488782} {:answer/id #uuid "f4732fd9-8b6b-5aea-b78d-38a224261978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21ed7e7e-47d0-51d4-9a00-b693a1f146e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488538} :answer-field/id #uuid "1448713c-4d53-5407-b118-7d28dec94eda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f502aa5-65d4-518a-a479-69aa4507aee1" :question/math-academy-id "q-223772" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are rational?\n\nI. $1.353124…$\n\nII. $1.5\\overset{―}{21}$\n\nIII. $4.055$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our numbers in turn.\n\n- $1.353124…$ is not a rational number. The notation \"$…$\" tells us that digits after the decimal point extend forever. However, there are no repeating digits.\n\n- $1.5\\overset{―}{21}$ is a rational number. The notation $\\overset{―}{21}$ tells us that the digits $2$ and $1$ after the decimal point repeat indefinitely.\n\n$$\n1.5\\overset{―}{21}=1.52121212121…\n$$\n\nAny decimal with repeating digits can be represented as a ratio of two integers. In this case,\n\n$$\n1.5\\overset{―}{21}=\\frac{1\\,506}{990}.\n$$\n\n- $4.055$ is a rational number because it can be expressed as a ratio of two integers:\n\n$$\n4.055=\\frac{4\\,055}{1\\,000}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Number as a Finite Decimal Using Long Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04347a2d-145f-5867-af0a-81fa8e5215a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488479} {:answer/id #uuid "13366131-125c-5a59-aef2-a9e4cddca9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488511} {:answer/id #uuid "aed5e85f-7dc7-56e5-b789-809f0ff7de15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488819} {:answer/id #uuid "c07e4f8c-5d1e-5065-a220-3cb84780f33f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488859} {:answer/id #uuid "fd3056ec-272c-5e42-83df-f6b93a425702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c07e4f8c-5d1e-5065-a220-3cb84780f33f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488859} :answer-field/id #uuid "f58fe76f-2951-521e-8878-70ddbf7d7041" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63a4febd-402b-590e-88f3-6d9132bd98e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-357033" :question/problem "Convert $\\frac{62}{5}$ into a decimal using long division." :question/worked-solution "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n62÷5\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0:$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,1\\,2\\,.\\,4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{6\\,\\phantom{|}2\\,.\\,0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{62}{5}=12.4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Number as a Finite Decimal Using Long Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66041baa-f2f5-5769-98db-319d1c73fe9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488665} {:answer/id #uuid "6d91651f-6d83-5f47-8942-47fc930c3fd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488684} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ce49d5-5b4e-5b2b-936f-1742a6f0f647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488869} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c605f9-5cc2-5bb2-9454-93d1b25d2c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488873} {:answer/id #uuid "f78c2d2e-1891-5609-8dfd-433b2e82611c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d91651f-6d83-5f47-8942-47fc930c3fd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488684} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc0168a1-6f55-5f37-b1c5-9ca0f0170bac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40ca59d6-4e89-5334-bddb-bed9c8ab1c58" :question/math-academy-id "q-357320" :question/problem "Convert $\\frac{74}{5}$ into a decimal using long division." :question/worked-solution "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n74÷5\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0:$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,1\\,4\\,.\\,8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{7\\,\\phantom{|}4\\,.\\,0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{74}{5}=14.8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Number as a Finite Decimal Using Long Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11feea40-5160-56af-ad40-07e554fbb357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488509} {:answer/id #uuid "6f4fee77-cc5f-5c32-92c1-5d9da6a5595e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.175" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488689} {:answer/id #uuid "afe14d7c-15c3-5d86-b336-862ca7b208d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488820} {:answer/id #uuid "cab7e5c7-e09b-56de-bfd0-7fce435a6db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.215" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488883} {:answer/id #uuid "e407094b-a9ef-5ee9-bcdb-94c0c5ae4c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e407094b-a9ef-5ee9-bcdb-94c0c5ae4c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488945} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae88c8ac-95f7-5200-b180-6af001020dfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ee55fb2d-2168-5fe7-9d4c-8b219d79c6ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-357330" :question/problem "Convert $\\frac{17}{8}$ into a decimal using long division." :question/worked-solution "To write down the given fraction as a decimal, we need to divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n17÷8\n$$\n\nWe proceed using the long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0:$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"5\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\,2\\,.\\,1\\,2\\,5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"5\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{1\\,\\phantom{|}7\\,.\\,0\\,\\phantom{|}0\\,\\phantom{|}0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{17}{8}=2.125.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489200 :knowledge-po