>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,⋮$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe could continue the division, but the same digit keeps repeating. Thus, the decimal continues with repeating $3$'s:\n\n$$\n5.833…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{35}{6}=5.833…=5.8\\overset{―}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Number as a Finite Decimal Using Long Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02051f35-0cee-5f86-b28e-bbe85e8e5e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488473} {:answer/id #